{# Used by all three /menu/ phases (browse, teach, drill) — restaurant
   name (centered) + a title/action row. The action itself (Train, "I'm
   Ready", or drill's "Back to Food") is passed in via {% call %} so the
   structure stays identical across every phase even though what's
   clickable differs by context — this is the one shared wrapper that
   replaced the old separate /learn/ page and its own divergent layout.

   showToggle renders the title as an in-page Food/Drinks dropdown
   instead of static text — both options always present, content-type
   filtered client-side (see menu-restaurant-filter.js), same mechanism
   as the sidemenu's restaurant switcher (no page reload, one file, no
   content duplication). /menu/food/, /menu/drinks/, and
   /menu/food/{category} (etc.) are real, independently-visitable routes
   via Netlify rewrites (netlify.toml, status 200 — not a redirect, so
   the URL bar keeps showing the route the visitor actually requested)
   that silently serve this same file; the page script reads the real
   URL on load to pick the right content type (and category, if present)
   on a direct visit. showToggle is omitted on teach/drill — mid-flow
   isn't the place to jump to the other content type, so those phases get
   a plain static (or, for drill, JS-filled — see nameId/titleId) title.

   nameId/titleId: drill is one shared dynamic block (not baked per
   category, since chat transcripts are inherently dynamic), so its
   restaurant name + Food/Drinks title can't be server-rendered per
   category like teach's can — these let the page script target and
   fill them in once a drill starts. #}
{% macro venueHeader(restaurantName, title, showToggle=false, nameId=false, titleId=false) %}
<p class="menu-review__venue-name"{% if nameId %} id="{{ nameId }}"{% endif %}>{{ restaurantName }}</p>
<div class="page-header">
  {% if showToggle %}
  <div class="page-title-switcher">
    <button class="page-title page-title-switcher__trigger" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Switch between Food and Drinks">
      <span class="page-title-switcher__label">{{ title }}</span>
      <span class="page-title-switcher__chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
    </button>
    <div class="content-type-switcher" hidden>
      <button class="content-type-switcher__option" type="button" data-content-type="food">Food</button>
      <button class="content-type-switcher__option" type="button" data-content-type="drink">Drinks</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% else %}
  <p class="page-title"{% if titleId %} id="{{ titleId }}"{% endif %}>{{ title }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {{ caller() }}
</div>
{% endmacro %}
